      "exposure": "National corrections policy from 2026 mandates hair cutting, hormone removal and psychiatric substitution described as conversion therapy, with denial of care. Immigration custody reports include forced labour, beatings, solitary confinement and severe sexual abuse of trans men.",
      "protection": "Not documented. No custody-specific remedy, placement protocol or prosecution for the reported abuse is documented; several executive orders are enjoined, but their application to these custody practices is not established.",
      "interaction": "Document, facilities or visa encounters can lead to detention, where the documented custody regime becomes the operative exposure.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "federal_state_facilities": {
      "exposure": "Federal policy bars use of government-funded single-sex facilities congruent with gender identity. Nationally, bans cover many states; four criminalise use in certain circumstances, with a documented trespass arrest and 24-hour men's-ward hold in one state. This state's inclusion in a ban map is not documented.",
      "protection": "State anti-discrimination law covers public accommodations since 2018 and public schools since 2019; the state highest court protected trans students on privacy grounds in 2024.",
      "interaction": "State protection operates in state and private settings, but does not cancel federal facilities or federal custody rules.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "care_services": {
      "exposure": "State bans on minors' gender-affirming medicine, surgery, puberty blockers, hormones and chest surgery took effect 2024-2026, with provider discipline and a private right to sue, even when medically judged necessary. National orders target minors' care and hospitals were subpoenaed for minor patients' records.",
      "protection": "State health-care anti-discrimination coverage began in 2020; a grandfather clause preserves treatment begun by 1 January 2026. No adult care ban in this state is documented.",
