      "exposure": "Care bans, provider discipline and right-to-sue exposure apply to families. A grades 5-12 girls' sports ban requires a birth certificate; its temporary stay means operative status is uncertain. Schools may investigate transition support, and parents may opt children out of gender-identity instruction.",
      "protection": "Grandfathering for existing care, a temporary sports-ban stay, a vetoed broader discrimination bill, and failed 2022 disclosure and conversion-repeal measures are documented.",
